<http://data.silknow.org/object/39fa244e-2854-3cff-8c4d-be6ffc421c4c/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Towel/Napkin, cotton embroidered with silk in double darning, double running in a line and musabak stitch, and metal thread in satin stitch and double darning on the diagonal (spaced, and with plate in satin stitch filling in squares.\nThe narrow border along either end has a horizontal line of metal thread above which are flowers in shaades of pink between clumps of three small cypress trees.  The main border has a series of lobed compartments outlined with metal thread.  Inside each is a striped blue bowl with green leaves, a large pink blossom and two pairs of other blossoms, also in pink. There are blue stripes towards the top of each compartment and between the compartments are sprays of small pink flowers.  \nOne side has been cut and hemmed"@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/39fa244e-2854-3cff-8c4d-be6ffc421c4c> .

<http://data.silknow.org/image/db1b259f-e608-3bdc-99fb-0dba10bf22bf>
